Suggests: openjdk-25-jre-headless
Description: web panel to install and manage Minecraft servers
 RedstonePanel deploys and manages Minecraft Java Edition and Bedrock Dedicated
 Server instances as systemd services on this host: start/stop, updates, live
 chat and console commands, a server.properties editor, player roles,
 reusable templates, world export and backups.
 .
 Sign in with a Linux account in the sudo or redstonepanel group, or with
 panel accounts managed in the panel. HTTPS and optional sign-in on the local
 network can be enabled by an admin in Panel Settings.
 .
 Java Edition servers need a Java runtime, and each Minecraft version needs a
 particular one (Java 25 for current releases, 21 for 1.20.5 to 1.21.x). The
 panel installs the openjdk-N-jre-headless a server needs when it's created,
 so hosts that only run Bedrock never get Java.
